# DIAL context-drift guardrail

## Mandatory context preflight

Before any material design, architecture, implementation, refactor or review:

1. Read `docs/project-truth/CONTEXT_BUNDLE.md`.
2. Read `docs/project-truth/project-truth.json`.
3. Read `docs/project-truth/feature-registry.json`.
4. Read `docs/project-truth/evidence-registry.json`.
5. Identify affected Feature IDs, their current gates and inherited evidence.
6. Identify relevant non-negotiable decision IDs.

Do not rely on remembered chat/session context when these files are available.

## Authority rule

The current machine-readable vNext.1 truth registry is the context anchor. Historical v4/Pack/companion documents remain detailed specifications only where not superseded.

If code, an old plan, a donor repo or a previous agent note conflicts with current project truth:

- do not average/merge the conflicting interpretations;
- do not silently choose the implementation that is easiest;
- current truth wins unless an explicit new decision is approved;
- record any approved change in the truth/feature/evidence registries in the same work unit.

## Evidence preservation

Accepted engineering evidence is durable project state.

- Never repeat E1a/E1b/E2a/E3a/E4a thin-slice stages merely because files or repositories moved.
- E6a retains inherited code evidence and begins at Integration Green after evidence normalization.
- E5a and OM-0 are new/unproven and begin at Thin Slice Required.
- Never downgrade a feature below the minimum gate asserted by accepted evidence without an explicit invalidation record explaining why the prior evidence is no longer representative.

## Feature preservation

A refactor, donor port, document rewrite or repo migration cannot silently remove functionality.

Before changing a feature family:

- identify its Feature Realization Contract / requirements;
- identify all applicable surfaces;
- preserve or deliberately supersede every requirement;
- update `feature-registry.json` when gate/status meaningfully changes.

## Integration context

Missing live credentials never means “stop development.”

- Continue fixture/contract/sandbox/key-ready implementation.
- Keep live/production evidence gates honestly open.
- Adding the eventual key must require configuration only, not feature code.

## Donor context

- FixItNow is the wholesale Dial a Tech application donor.
- PORT-WHOLESALE means preserve the mature application/UI structure, then replace donor SoRs with DIAL contracts.
- Donor auth, payments, jobs, catalogue, delivery, tax and storage never silently become DIAL authority.
- Record donor revision/licence/adaptation boundary in the work evidence.

## Frontend context

Do not let a new agent reinterpret frontend requirements as “make something modern.”

For material UI work, retain:

- user outcome and workflow;
- branch visual identity;
- reference/Figma/design-system context;
- required screen states;
- visual evidence and accessibility criteria.

Generic AI-generated screens are a context-drift failure because they discard intentional product/design decisions.

## Checkpoints

Checkpoint context after:

- new architecture decision;
- feature scope change;
- donor/adaptor substitution;
- release-gate movement;
- new accepted evidence;
- new external dependency;
- major UI/art-direction change.

At handoff/end of session, use `docs/project-truth/SESSION_HANDOFF_TEMPLATE.md`.

## Drift tripwires

Immediately run `dial-context-drift-check` if work proposes or implies any of:

- DIAL-owned/principal Spare inventory;
- AI binding payable amounts or ledger writes;
- unofficial WhatsApp;
- a second money/job/delivery/catalogue SoR;
- Fixture == Production Green;
- missing API key == engineering blocker;
- a repeated inherited thin slice;
- generic cross-branch storefront skin;
- cheap recreation replacing FixItNow wholesale;
- Opportunity Marketplace creating a parallel post-award Job/Payment system;
- removing an accepted feature because it is inconvenient during migration/refactor.

## Required command

Run `pnpm context:check` before merge or any claim that a significant feature/gate is complete.
